# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 usual.cc ln and sqrt: ln(inv(f)) returns -ln(f) and sqrt(inv(f)) returns inv(sqrt(f)) for any f, identities that fail on the negative real axis, where they give the conjugate of the principal value: ln(1/(1-sqrt(2))) = -ln(1-sqrt(2)), evalf 0.88137358702-3.14159265359*i (right 0.88137358702+3.14159265359*i), sqrt(1/(pi-4)) = 1/sqrt(pi-4), evalf -1.07932761087*i (right +1.07932761087*i); also sec and csc of an angle where cos or sin is negative (sqrt(sec(2)) = 1/sqrt(cos(2)), ln(sec(2)) = -ln(cos(2))), log10 through ln, and ln of the fraction 1/-2 that inv(-2) and a subst give (ln(inv(-2)) = -ln(-2)). Now the rule is skipped where f has a numeric value (has_evalf) or is a bare name, and sign(f) is -1 (sign(1-sqrt(2)), sign(cos(2)), an assumed x<0), and for a fraction 1/d with d < 0 in ln; ln and sqrt keep inv(f) and evalf gives the principal value. A free expression and an undecided sign keep the rewrite (ln(1/x) = -ln(x), sqrt(1/x) = 1/sqrt(x)).
